{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghpk6uNwtnSfVrcU7LLt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Setup.** In a tetrahedral d⁸ ion the ground term is ³T₁(F). The two excited terms observed here are ³T₂(F) and the upper ³T₁, which is mainly ³T₁(P). The ³T₁(F) and ³T₁(P) terms mix through an off-diagonal element of 6B.\n\nEnergies relative to the free-ion F barycentre:\n- ³T₂ = +2Dq\n- ³T₁(F) and ³T₁(P) come from the matrix [[−6Dq, 6B], [6B, 15B]]. The lower root E₁ is the ground state, and the upper root E₂ is the ³T₁(2) state.\n\n**Equations.**\n- ν₁ = ³T₂ − E₁ = 4400, so E₁ = 2Dq − 4400.\n- ν₂ = E₂ − E₁ = 15500, so E₂ = 2Dq + 11100.\n\nThe trace of the matrix gives E₁ + E₂ = 15B − 6Dq. Substituting the two expressions above:\n- 4Dq + 6700 = 15B − 6Dq, so B = (10Dq + 6700)/15.\n\nThe determinant gives E₁E₂ = −90Dq·B − 36B². Substituting B and expanding:\n- 80Dq² + 75040Dq − 41.66×10⁶ = 0, which simplifies to Dq² + 938Dq − 520720 = 0.\n\nThe positive root is Dq ≈ 392 cm⁻¹. Then B = (3916 + 6700)/15 ≈ 708 cm⁻¹.\n\n**C.** The assumed ratio C/B = 4.5 gives C ≈ 3185 cm⁻¹. It does not enter the ³T terms used here, so it does not affect Dq or B.\n\n**Result:** Dq ≈ 392 cm⁻¹ and B ≈ 708 cm⁻¹. B is about 70% of the free-ion value for Ni²⁺, which is reasonable for an oxide.\n\n{\"Dq\": 392, \"B\": 708, \"C\": 3185, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Solved the tetrahedral d8 ³T₁(F)–³T₁(P) 2x2 matrix with ³T₂ at 2Dq; C follows from the assumed C/B = 4.5.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":845,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":845,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"31a7